# OPENRCT2

/sdl

###############
## OpenRCT2mini-specific
###############

# Cross-build output dirs (the host build dir is build-host*; ARM is build-arm).
# Upstream's `[Bb]uild/` rule below catches plain "build/" but not the hyphenated
# variants we use.
/build-arm/
/build-host/
/build-host-i686/
/build-asan/

# Internal planning documents — design plans, audits, peer-reviews, phase
# progress logs, perf reports. Kept on disk so the dev can reference them
# locally without committing scratch reasoning into git history. Anything
# user-facing (readme.md, CONTRIBUTING.md, CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md, contributors.md,
# THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md) doesn't match these patterns and stays tracked.
/*-plan.md
/*-plan-review.md
/*-audit.md
/phase-*.md
/perf-report-*.md
/OpenRCT2mini-Plan.md

# Local game-data installs used for on-host testing. RCT1 / RCT2 are
# Chris Sawyer / Atari / Infogrames property — not redistributable. The user
# of an OpenRCT2mini build supplies their own legitimate copies (see readme.md).
/gamedata/

# Sprite dumps extracted from g1.dat / g2.dat for visual reference during UI
# work (cut 50 / Rumble Editor v2.12 / etc.). They originate from the
# proprietary game data and are not redistributable.
/ui_art/

# Cursor PNG working set (cut 50). The cursor bitmaps were extracted from
# OpenRCT2's CursorData.cpp as PNGs to allow round-trip editing; the
# canonical source of truth is the X-bitmap arrays in CursorData.cpp itself.
# These PNGs are scratch material — re-extractable, not the build input.
/cursors/all/

# Build / packaging logs and per-revision dumps generated under dist/.
# (dist/ itself is excluded by upstream below, but make the intent explicit
# here so anyone reading just this section sees what's stripped.)
/dist/
*.log

# Local toolchain probe output.
/dist/cut*.txt

# Compiled dll
openrct2.dll

# Distribution
distribution/windows/*.exe
distribution/android/*/external/

# Build artifacts
artifacts
bin.*/
.cache
.dependencies
sequencesversion
objectsversion
/out/

#lib
lib
libversion

# Downloaded or built data files
data/g2.dat
data/fonts.dat
data/palettes.dat
data/tracks.dat
data/sequence
data/object
data/assetpack
test/tests/testdata/replays
test/tests/testdata/sprites/result.dat

